 learn choosing a research topic through explicit strategy, worked examples and evidence-based practice. Identify purpose and audience, apply a clear process, check work against criteria and explain choices with textual or factual support. Keep school-safe topics; credit sources; do not invent NESA content points beyond catalogue codes.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Thinking choosing a research topic is only talent or first-draft luck. Explicit process, evidence and revision produce reliable Year 7 work. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Choosing a research topic.","caption":"See the process.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Teach</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">what/why/how</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Model</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">worked example</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.","who"